        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-20T15:17:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I honestly think that\u0027s actually a good thing. From a build perspective, a node in a build graph should not know where it goes to. It cares about itself and the subgraph rooted at it. This creates a nice abstraction and avoids long-term scalability issues (e.g. it\u0027d be a disaster if java_libraries in google3 knew which binaries depend on them).\n\nWe have to do checks in two different places regardless: one for APKs and one for APEXes, right? Unless there is a way to move this to ApexModule (we\u0027ll need to have updatable prop there and checkStableSdkVersion method shared)? I guess this is partially why I am considering moving SdkContext to a common place as well..",
      "parentUuid": "5888e815_a7b95606",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1940,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 1940,
        "endChar": 21
      },
